f_epa_per_play":0.01481}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.5713,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"HOU","distance":0.6026,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Bobby Slowik"},{"season":2025,"team":"NE","distance":0.7238,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Josh McDaniels"},{"season":2023,"team":"HOU","distance":0.7452,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Bobby Slowik"},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.7642,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"BAL","distance":1.254,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Mike Macdonald"},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":1.26,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"ARI","distance":1.276,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Nick Rallis"},{"season":2018,"team":"BAL","distance":1.287,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"DET","distance":1.323,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Vikings went 14-3 in 2024 and outscored opponents 432 to 332. The defense did most of the work, finishing 3rd in EPA allowed while the offense ranked 15th in EPA per play. Their most distinctive traits were the 2nd highest under center rate and the lowest Cover 1 rate in the league.","offense":"The Vikings offense was about average by EPA per play. They threw more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score did not call for it. Schematically, they stood out for the 2nd highest under center rate and the 2nd highest under center rate in the league. Sam Darnold ran the passing game and leaned heavily on Justin Jefferson, who drew 30% of the targets.","defense":"The Vikings had one of the best defenses in the league, ranking 6th or better in all five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area was takeaways per game, where it led the league, and it had no real weak spot. Jonathan Greenard led the team with 12 sacks, and Andrew Van Ginkel added 11.5, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they had the lowest Cover 1 rate in the league.","special":"The Vikings were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 83% of field goals, which was a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 9% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Sam Darnold played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,319 yards. Justin Jefferson was the clear top target with 30% of the looks and 1,533 receiving yards. Aaron Jones handled most of the work in the backfield with 66% of the carries. On defense, Jonathan Greenard led the team with 12 sacks and Byron Murphy picked off 6 passes.","coaching":"Kevin O'Connell called the offense as head coach and Brian Flores called the defense. Their offense looked most like the 2023 Raiders and the 2024 Texans under Bobby Slowik. Their defense looked most like the 2022 Ravens under Mike Macdonald and the 2022 Packers.","trends":"The offense went from 17th in EPA per play in 2023 to 15th in 2024, about where it was. The defense moved from 20th in EPA allowed per play in 2023 to 3rd in 2024, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was 2-Man rate, which went from 2% to 10%.","notes":"Every data source is available for 2024. This season uses the newer formation labels, which group singleback, I formation and empty sets together as under center, so those older formation rates are not shown."}}